<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59079" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρδαξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱκος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cordax</i>, a dance of the old Comedy, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρδακα ἑλκύσαι</span> to dance <i>it</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				540
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				555
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Salt.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχεῖσθαι νήφων τὸν κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					6.3
				</span></i>
			; regarded as indecent, l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.631d
			</span></i>; also in cult of Artemis at Sipylus, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				6.22.1
			</span></i>; at Elis, ibid.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ περὶ τὸν Πύθιον Ἀπόλλωνα κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(7).246
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>).</div>
